    "SKILL.md": "---\nname: self-learning-agent\ndescription: Continuously improve performance through plan-act-reflect loops, using outcomes to adapt strategy and behavior over time. Use whenever the user wants autonomous iteration, error-driven learning, or measurable self-improvement across repeated tasks.\n---\n\n# Self-Learning Agent\n\nA skill for autonomous, iterative improvement.\n\nUse this when the task benefits from short repeated cycles where the agent:\n\n- sets a hypothesis,\n- takes action,\n- evaluates outcomes,\n- updates strategy,\n- and repeats across turns until success criteria are met or stop criteria apply.\n\n## Timeout Guard\n\n- Timebox to at most 2 short cycles in one turn.\n- Pick the smallest high-signal action first.\n- Stop exploration once the working set is sufficient.\n- Validate outcome with available checks, then finalize.\n- Prefer a concise completion message over long reflection.\n\n## Common Operating Principles\n\n- Read only the docs/context required to execute correctly before acting.\n- Follow the user instruction exactly; avoid paraphrase and unrequested improvements.\n- Keep scope surgical: change only what the request names.\n- Verify outcomes using available checks/tests; do not rely on intuition.\n- Keep communication concise and direct.\n- Prefer fewer, bundled tool invocations over fragmented calls.\n- If a persistent note surface exists, leave a short generalized note for future runs.\n\n## Learning Principles\n\n- **Evidence over intuition:** prefer observed outcomes over confidence.\n- **Short feedback loops:** many small cycles beat one large speculative pass.\n- **Explicit memory:** write down lessons so they transfer to future runs.\n- **Error as signal:** failures are training data, not dead ends.\n- **Generalization over overfitting:** optimize for recurring patterns, not one-off wins.\n\n## When to Stop\n\nStop iterating when one of the following is true:\n- success criteria are met,\n- marginal gains are consistently low,\n- constraints prevent further useful progress,\n- or the user chooses to finalize.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not fabricate results or hidden evidence.\n- Do not claim learning without measurable or observable change.\n- Do not run risky or irreversible operations without explicit user consent.\n- Do not optimize for vanity metrics that do not map to user value.\n\n## Trigger Examples\n\nThis skill should trigger for prompts like:\n- \"Keep trying until the approach converges; learn from each failed attempt.\"\n- \"Build this in iterations and improve accuracy each round.\"\n- \"Run a feedback loop and optimize based on observed errors.\"\n- \"Act like an autonomous agent that self-corrects over time.\""
